Fix SSC sensor startup race: start polling for clients that claimed during discovery
Upstream 3.9 owns the D-Bus name before find_sensors() completes. A claim that
arrives during the multi-second SSC discovery window inserts the client but
cannot start polling (no driver yet), and initial-scan sensors never emit a
hotplug uevent, so the sensor never starts. Mirror the hotplug path in
name_acquired_handler(): start polling for driver types that already have
claimants once discovery finishes.
--- a/src/iio-sensor-proxy.c
+++ b/src/iio-sensor-proxy.c
+++ iio-sensor-proxy-3.9/src/iio-sensor-proxy.c	2026-09-06 19:03:38.312995058 +0200
@@ -784,6 +784,21 @@
 	if (!any_sensors_left (data))
 		goto bail;
 
+	/* Clients that claimed a sensor while discovery was still running
+	 * (possible because the D-Bus name is owned before find_sensors()
+	 * completes) never got their driver started: there was no driver yet
+	 * at claim time, and sensors found by the initial scan do not
+	 * generate a hotplug uevent. Start polling for those clients now,
+	 * mirroring what the hotplug path does. */
+	for (i = 0; i < NUM_SENSOR_TYPES; i++) {
+		if (DEVICE_FOR_TYPE(i) && g_hash_table_size (data->clients[i]) > 0) {
+			g_debug ("Starting driver for clients that claimed the %s sensor during startup",
+				 driver_type_to_str (i));
+			data->sensor_startup_dbus_event_delayed[i] = TRUE;
+			driver_set_polling (DEVICE_FOR_TYPE(i), TRUE);
+		}
+	}
+
 	send_dbus_event (data, PROP_ALL);
 	send_dbus_event (data, PROP_ALL_COMPASS);
 	return;
